        google: { rating: 4.2, review_count: 209, maps_url: 'https://maps.google.com/?cid=6765514405281286692&g_mp=CiVnb29nbGUubWFwcy5wbGFjZXMudjEuUGxhY2VzLkdldFBsYWNlEAIYBCAA', reviews: [{author: 'Kai Haase', rating: 5, text: 'I love stopping by Legacy! Everyone is so friendly and very knowledgeable. I especially appreciate Melanie’s insight— They always help make deciding between so many options less overwhelming. I can tell they’re very passionate about it and I appreciate the joy they bring! I also love how honest they are about what is in store and what to look forward to, if there’s something specific I ask about.', time: '5 months ago'}, {author: 'James Barstow', rating: 2, text: 'Decent spot with a cool mural and a vibe similar to Fire Station in Michigan. Service is quick and the budtenders are friendly, though they mostly stick to the "indica = in da couch" basics.  ​My main hang-up is the loyalty program. They’ve been open for about 6 months now,  yet the staff still says they have no clue what the points are actually for. My fiance has over 1,600 points saved up, and i', time: '6 months ago'}, {author: 'Shawn Christopherson', rating: 5, text: 'Maleek and Jules (hope I got the names correct) were very welcoming, informative and helpful and getting me what I need. Amazing service can\'t wait to try my Frankenstein product!', time: '2 months ago'}, {author: 'Dylan Fisher', rating: 5, text: 'Great atmosphere as well as knowledgeable staff make this a frontier location for this budding new business in D-Town. Lacy was not only helpful but also seemed to be particularly enthusiastic with assisting me with any suggestions or questions I had in mind. Glad to see MN is getting on track with the times, catching up to pace with several other states, and providing employment via places like L', time: '4 months ago'}, {author: 'Tina Marie', rating: 3, text: 'This place was nice, awesome wall murals, very friendly staff at the counter. My only issues was at the door it states the different type of IDs needed to get past and Tribal ID was at the top of that list. I handed the young man working my Tribal ID, he looked at it and said this do you have something else? I told him this is a Federal Accepted ID but he continued to tell me it would take to long', time: 'a year ago'}] }
